From: lucaszhongsj <lucaszhongsj@foxmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 14:37:26 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] tools/companion_pins: check the module's pins against a
 rewritten image

The ACNH module reads the guest through fixed main-relative addresses, and its
pins record the words expected there: a build whose words differ closes the
module's domains, and an empty band is the only symptom. The tool parses the
two .inc files, reads the 32-bit little-endian words at each offset from a
patched main image, and fails on a differing word, a pin past the image's end,
a line that is not a pin, a .inc generated from another build, or an image
whose build cannot be read at all. The build ID is the one patch_nso.py writes
in main.cuts.tsv beside the image; the image is a raw module, not an NSO
header, so it comes from there and not from the file's bytes.

All 91 pins (49 in acnh_live_pins.inc, 42 in acnh_bag_pins.inc) match build
ff1d1c05670db6021c85b624a710b963, and the game note records the command that
repeats the check. The image is read with seeks rather than whole: a patched
main runs to hundreds of megabytes. The tests use synthetic images and pin
files, so they need no game files; the tool needs them to be useful, not to be
imported.

Not checked: lint_python.py, which has no venv with the pinned lint
requirements on this machine.

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: The ACNH companion's pins: a tool that checks a rewritten image and the pack step that refuses one they were not found on; nxnative carries them on feat/acnh-companion
Issue: none yet: no upstream issue for the companion

